### Wallet Transfer Service — example requests.
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or copy into curl.
### Start the server first:  make run   (in-memory store, no DB needed)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Create source wallet with an opening balance of 1000.
### The server generates the id and returns it in the body and Location header.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "openingBalance": 1000,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Create destination wallet with an opening balance of 0.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "openingBalance": 0,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Create a transfer (first call -> 201 Created, status PROCESSED).
### Replace the wallet ids below with the ids returned by the calls above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "abc123",
  "fromWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID",
  "toWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_DEST_WALLET_ID",
  "amount": 100
}

### Replay the SAME request (same key + params) -> 200 OK, same transfer, no double spend
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "abc123",
  "fromWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID",
  "toWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_DEST_WALLET_ID",
  "amount": 100
}

### Reuse the key with DIFFERENT params -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "abc123",
  "fromWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID",
  "toWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_DEST_WALLET_ID",
  "amount": 500
}

### Transfer that exceeds the balance -> 201 Created, status FAILED (no ledger entries)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "overdraw-1",
  "fromWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_DEST_WALLET_ID",
  "toWalletId": "REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID",
  "amount": 999999
}

### Get a transfer by id (replace with an id returned above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers/REPLACE_WITH_TRANSFER_ID

### Get a wallet (shows current balance)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID

### Get a wallet's double-entry ledger history (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallets/REPLACE_WITH_SOURCE_WALLET_ID/ledger
